{"id":"c1","verdict":"keep","level":"E1","checks":{"subject":true,"predicate":true,"arguments":true,"time":true,"polarity":true,"modality":true,"informative":true},"evidence":[{"turn_id":1,"quote":"You look depressed"}],"basis":"A directly observes B's appearance as depressed; 'You look' is a perceptual predicate about B.","alternative":"","replacement":null},
{"id":"c2","verdict":"repair","level":"E2","checks":{"subject":true,"predicate":true,"arguments":true,"time":true,"polarity":true,"modality":true,"informative":false},"evidence":[{"turn_id":3,"quote":"taught him a lesson for you"}],"basis":"'for you' presupposes B has an issue with 'him' (wronged), but 'would like taught a lesson' overstates certainty since A is asking a question; B has not confirmed desire.","alternative":"B might not want the lesson taught; A is merely offering.","replacement":{"claim":"B has an issue with a male third party ('him') whom A offers to teach a lesson for B.","attribute":"grievance_against_third_party","mechanism":"presupposition of 'for you' in an offer implies B has a complaint about 'him'","evidence":[{"turn_id":3,"quote":"taught him a lesson for you"}]}},
{"id":"c3","verdict":"keep","level":"E1","checks":{"subject":true,"predicate":true,"arguments":true,"time":true,"polarity":true,"modality":true,"informative":true},"evidence":[{"turn_id":1,"quote":"You look depressed"}],"basis":"Same as c1; direct perceptual description of B by A.","alternative":"","replacement":null},
{"id":"c4","verdict":"keep","level":"E2","checks":{"subject":true,"predicate":true,"arguments":true,"time":true,"polarity":true,"modality":true,"informative":true},"evidence":[{"turn_id":3,"quote":"taught him a lesson for you"}],"basis":"'teach him a lesson for you' presupposes 'him' wronged B; 'for you' attaches the benefit to B, implying B is the aggrieved party.","alternative":"","replacement":null},
{"id":"c5","verdict":"reject","level":"E4","checks":{"subject":true,"predicate":false,"arguments":true,"time":true,"polarity":true,"modality":false,"informative":true},"evidence":[{"turn_id":3,"quote":"Would you rather I taught him a lesson for you"}],"basis":"A is asking a question ('Would you rather'); B has not confirmed wanting retribution. The modality is interrogative, not declarative. The unknown answer to the question is not evidence of B's desire.","alternative":"B might decline the offer; A is merely proposing an option.","replacement":null}
]}
